# Portal UX copy

The portal is for **builders and demo audiences**, not engine contributors reading
source. Labels, hints, and governance rails should explain **what they get**, not
**how the engine implements it**.

## Do not surface in the UI

- README mechanics (for example `## Provenance`, “synced on generate”, Jinja
  section names, or `provenance_readme.py` behavior).
- Internal module or function names, gate runner steps, or Copier/render pipeline
  jargon unless the user must run a CLI command.
- Roadmap theme labels, semver planning names, or “shipped in v1.x” in product
  chrome (OK in `docs/`, not in templates).

## Prefer instead

- **Lineage:** blueprint@version, pinned standard, governance baseline, engine version.
  Provenance is written to `repave.yaml` in the artifact — do not use the word
  “receipt” in templates or show a full-file YAML dump on the result page (lineage
  rows are enough; file tree still lists `repave.yaml`).
- **Policy:** profile label, pack source, catalog rule titles — not raw skip-check
  wiring unless troubleshooting.
- **Gates:** gate id and pass/fail/skip; failures get human lead-ins (for example
  “Publish blocked”) then tool output in expandable excerpts.
- **Backstage:** `catalog-info.yaml`, owner, `repave.dev/*` annotations — product
  integration language from `docs/backstage.md`.

## When adding governance or result panels

- Match wording across `blueprint_form.html` (governance rail) and `result.html`
  (lineage block): same terms for standard, policy, and provenance file.
- If copy would only make sense to someone who read `engine/src/repave_engine/`,
  rewrite it or move it to `docs/` / code comments.

## Review checklist (portal PRs)

- [ ] No README section headers or “sync on generate” phrasing in templates/JS.
- [ ] Hints explain user action or outcome, not internal sync/render steps.
- [ ] New strings are consistent with `docs/portal-design.md` (Copy and voice).
- [ ] **Behavior unchanged:** plan (dry-run) and scaffold still reach `/generate`
  and show results — see `portal-ui-behavior.mdc`.
- [ ] Copy/label renames update tests in `engine/tests/test_api.py` in the same PR.
